{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determine whether the decimal representation of an integer consists of\n    exactly two distinct digits that strictly alternate.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A signed 64\u2011bit integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the absolute value of n has two distinct digits that\n        alternate without any equal adjacent digits, otherwise False.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer\")\n\n    s = str(abs(n))\n    if len(s) <= 1:\n        return False\n\n    digit1 = None\n    digit2 = None\n    prev = None\n\n    for ch in s:\n        if prev is None:\n            digit1 = ch\n            prev = ch\n            continue\n\n        if ch == prev:\n            return False\n\n        if digit1 is None:\n            digit1 = ch\n        elif digit2 is None:\n            if ch != digit1:\n                digit2 = ch\n        else:\n            if ch != digit1:\n                return False\n\n        prev = ch\n\n    return digit2 is not None"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/93", "solution": "def power(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute a raised to the power b (a^b).\n\n    Parameters:\n        a (int): Base value. Can be negative, zero, or positive.\n        b (int): Non\u2011negative exponent. Must satisfy b >= 0.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The integer result of a**b.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If b is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if b < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Exponent must be non\u2011negative\")\n    result = 1\n    base = a\n    exp = b\n    while exp:\n        if exp & 1:\n            result *= base\n        base *= base\n        exp >>= 1\n    return result"}
