{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "from collections.abc import Iterable\nfrom typing import Any, List\ndef common_in_nested_lists(data: Iterable[Iterable[Any]]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a sorted list of elements common to all inner iterables.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    data : Iterable[Iterable[Any]]\n        An outer iterable containing inner iterables (e.g., lists, tuples, sets, generators).\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    List[Any]\n        A list of elements present in every inner iterable, sorted in ascending order.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If `data` is not iterable.\n        If any inner element is not iterable.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> common_in_nested_lists([[1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4], [0, 2, 3]])\n    [2, 3]\n    >>> common_in_nested_lists(({'a', 'b'}, {'b', 'c'}))\n    ['b']\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, Iterable):\n        raise TypeError(\"data must be an iterable of iterables\")\n\n    outer_iter = iter(data)\n    try:\n        first_inner = next(outer_iter)\n    except StopIteration:\n        return []\n\n    if not isinstance(first_inner, Iterable):\n        raise TypeError(f\"inner element {first_inner!r} is not iterable\")\n\n    common_set = set(first_inner)\n\n    for inner in outer_iter:\n        if not isinstance(inner, Iterable):\n            raise TypeError(f\"inner element {inner!r} is not iterable\")\n        common_set.intersection_update(inner)\n        if not common_set:\n            return []\n\n    return sorted(common_set)"}
