{"task_id": "Mbpp/116", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\ndef tuple_to_int(numbers: Tuple[int, ...]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Concatenate the decimal representation of a tuple of positive integers into a single integer.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers: A tuple containing positive integers (each >= 1). An empty tuple is allowed.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The integer formed by concatenating the decimal strings of the numbers in order.\n            Returns 0 if the input tuple is empty.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any element in ``numbers`` is not an integer greater than or equal to 1.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> tuple_to_int((12, 34, 5))\n        12345\n        >>> tuple_to_int((7,))\n        7\n        >>> tuple_to_int(())\n        0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    for n in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"All elements must be positive integers; got {n!r}\")\n\n    concatenated = \"\".join(str(n) for n in numbers)\n    return int(concatenated)"}
