{"task_id": "Mbpp/234", "solution": "def volume_cube(side: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the volume of a cube.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    side : float or int\n        The length of one side of the cube. Must be non\u2011negative.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    float\n        The volume of the cube.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If `side` is not an int or float.\n    ValueError\n        If `side` is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(side, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(f\"side must be int or float, got {type(side).__name__}\")\n    if side < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"side must be non-negative\")\n    return float(side ** 3)"}
