{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "from collections import defaultdict\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Tuple\ndef _normalize_pair(pair: Tuple[Any, Any]) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return the pair with the smaller element first.\"\"\"\n    a, b = pair\n    return pair if a <= b else (b, a)\ndef check_occurences(pairs: List[Tuple[Any, Any]]) -> Dict[Tuple[Any, Any], int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count occurrences of unordered 2\u2011element tuples.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    pairs : List[Tuple[Any, Any]]\n        List of 2\u2011element tuples. Elements must be hashable and comparable for ordering.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    Dict[Tuple[Any, Any], int]\n        Dictionary mapping each unique unordered tuple (with the smaller element first) to its occurrence count.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If any element is not a 2\u2011element tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    counter: Dict[Tuple[Any, Any], int] = defaultdict(int)\n\n    for pair in pairs:\n        if not isinstance(pair, tuple) or len(pair) != 2:\n            raise TypeError(\n                f\"All items must be 2\u2011element tuples; invalid item: {pair!r}\"\n            )\n        key = _normalize_pair(pair)\n        counter[key] += 1\n\n    return dict(counter)"}
