{"task_id": "Mbpp/276", "solution": "import math\ndef volume_cylinder(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the volume of a right circular cylinder.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    radius : float\n        Radius of the cylinder (must be non-negative).\n    height : float\n        Height of the cylinder (must be non-negative).\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    float\n        The volume computed as \u03c0 * r\u00b2 * h.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If radius or height are not real numbers or are negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"radius must be a real number\")\n    if not isinstance(height, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"height must be a real number\")\n    if radius < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"radius must be non-negative\")\n    if height < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"height must be non-negative\")\n\n    return math.pi * radius ** 2 * height"}
