{"task_id": "Mbpp/412", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef remove_odd(input_list: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list containing only even integers from the input list.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    input_list : list[int]\n        A list of integers to filter. Must be a list and all elements must be integers.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list[int]\n        A new list containing only the even integers from `input_list`, preserving order.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If `input_list` is not a list or contains non-integer elements.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> remove_odd([1, 2, 3])\n    [2]\n    >>> remove_odd([])\n    []\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(input_list)\n    return _filter_even_numbers(input_list)\ndef _filter_even_numbers(input_list: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    return [x for x in input_list if x % 2 == 0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/413", "solution": "from typing import Any, List, Tuple\ndef extract_nth_element(data: List[Tuple[Any, ...]], n: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract the nth element from each tuple in a list.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    data : List[Tuple[Any, ...]]\n        List containing tuples of arbitrary length.\n    n : int\n        Zero-based index of the element to extract.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    List[Any]\n        List of the nth elements from each tuple.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If n is negative, or if n is greater than or equal to the length of any tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Index n must be non\u2011negative.\")\n    result: List[Any] = []\n    for idx, tup in enumerate(data):\n        if n >= len(tup):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Index {n} out of range for tuple at position {idx} with length {len(tup)}.\"\n            )\n        result.append(tup[n])\n    return result"}
