{"task_id": "Mbpp/439", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef multiple_to_single(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Concatenates a list of non\u2011negative integers into a single integer.\n\n    Parameters:\n        numbers (List[int]): List of non\u2011negative integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The concatenated integer. Returns 0 for an empty list.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any integer is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n    string_parts = []\n    for number in numbers:\n        if number < 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Negative number encountered: {number}\")\n        string_parts.append(str(number))\n    concatenated = \"\".join(string_parts)\n    return int(concatenated)"}
