{"task_id": "Mbpp/456", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef reverse_string_list(strings: List[str]) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return a new list with each input string reversed.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    strings : List[str]\n        A list containing string elements.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    List[str]\n        A new list where each string is reversed. The original order of\n        elements is preserved.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If `strings` is not a list or any element in `strings` is not a string.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> reverse_string_list(['hello', 'world'])\n    ['olleh', 'dlrow']\n    >>> reverse_string_list([])\n    []\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation\n    if not isinstance(strings, list):\n        raise TypeError(f\"Expected a list, got {type(strings).__name__}\")\n\n    for idx, s in enumerate(strings):\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {idx} is not a string (type: {type(s).__name__})\")\n\n    # Reverse each string\n    return [s[::-1] for s in strings]"}
