{"task_id": "Mbpp/569", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef sort_sublists(data: List[List[str]]) -> List[List[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list of lists where each inner list is sorted\n    alphabetically (ascending, case\u2011sensitive).  The original\n    data structure is left unmodified.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    data : List[List[str]]\n        Outer list of strings.  Each element must be a list of strings\n        and no inner element may itself be a list.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    List[List[str]]\n        New list with the same outer length as *data* where each inner\n        list is sorted.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If *data* is not a list, if any sublist is not a list,\n        or if any element within a sublist is not a string.\n    ValueError\n        If any sublist contains a nested list (depth > 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise TypeError(f\"Expected outer list, got {type(data).__name__}\")\n\n    result = []\n    for idx_outer, sub in enumerate(data):\n        if not isinstance(sub, list):\n            raise TypeError(\n                f\"Expected list of strings at index {idx_outer}, \"\n                f\"got {type(sub).__name__}\"\n            )\n        # Validate sublist contents and check for deep nesting\n        for idx_inner, item in enumerate(sub):\n            if isinstance(item, list):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"Deep nesting detected at index {idx_outer}, sub-index {idx_inner}\"\n                )\n            if not isinstance(item, str):\n                raise TypeError(\n                    f\"Expected string at index {idx_outer}, sub-index {idx_inner}, \"\n                    f\"got {type(item).__name__}\"\n                )\n        # Create a sorted copy of the sublist\n        sorted_sub = sorted(sub)\n        result.append(sorted_sub)\n\n    return result"}
