{"task_id": "Mbpp/573", "solution": "from typing import Iterable\ndef unique_product(lst: Iterable[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the product of unique integers in the provided iterable.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    lst : Iterable[int]\n        An iterable containing integer values.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        The product of the distinct integers in `lst`. Returns 1 if `lst`\n        contains no elements.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> unique_product([10, 20, 30, 40, 20, 50, 60, 40])\n    720000000\n    \"\"\"\n    seen: set[int] = set()\n    product: int = 1\n    for val in lst:\n        if val not in seen:\n            product *= val\n            seen.add(val)\n    return product"}
