{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "def last_Digit_Factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the last decimal digit of n! (n factorial).\n\n    Parameters:\n        n (int): Non\u2011negative integer whose factorial's last digit is required.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The last digit of n!.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non\u2011negative\")\n    if n >= 5:\n        return 0\n    # Precomputed last digits for 0! through 4!\n    return [1, 1, 2, 6, 4][n] % 10  # 6 % 10 = 6, 4 % 10 = 4"}
