{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "def find_dissimilar(t1: tuple, t2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a tuple of elements that are present in exactly one of the two input tuples.\n\n    The function performs an order\u2011preserving asymmetric difference between `t1` and `t2`.  \n    Elements that appear in `t1` but not in `t2` are listed first, followed by elements that\n    appear in `t2` but not in `t1`. The relative order of appearance from the original tuples\n    is maintained.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    t1 : tuple\n        First input tuple containing hashable elements.\n    t2 : tuple\n        Second input tuple containing hashable elements.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    tuple\n        A tuple containing the dissimilar elements, preserving the order of appearance.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If either `t1` or `t2` is not a tuple.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> find_dissimilar((1, 2, 3), (3, 4, 5))\n    (1, 2, 4, 5)\n\n    >>> find_dissimilar(('a', 'b'), ('b', 'c'))\n    ('a', 'c')\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(t1, tuple) or not isinstance(t2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both arguments must be tuples.\")\n\n    set_t1 = set(t1)\n    set_t2 = set(t2)\n\n    result = [elem for elem in t1 if elem not in set_t2]\n    result.extend([elem for elem in t2 if elem not in set_t1])\n\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/580", "solution": "from typing import Tuple, Any\ndef extract_even(data: Tuple[Any, ...]) -> Tuple[Any, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Recursively removes odd integers from nested tuples.\n\n    Parameters:\n        data (Tuple[Any, ...]): A tuple that may contain integers or other nested tuples.\n\n    Returns:\n        Tuple[Any, ...]: A new tuple with the same structure, containing only even integers.\n                         Empty tuples are omitted.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If `data` is not a tuple or contains elements that are not\n                   integers or tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple\")\n    result = []\n    for item in data:\n        if isinstance(item, int):\n            if item % 2 == 0:\n                result.append(item)\n        elif isinstance(item, tuple):\n            sub = extract_even(item)\n            if sub:\n                result.append(sub)\n        else:\n            raise TypeError(\"Tuple elements must be ints or tuples\")\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/581", "solution": "def surface_Area(base_edge, height):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate total surface area of a square pyramid.\n\n    Surface Area = base_edge^2 + 2 * base_edge * height\n\n    Parameters:\n        base_edge (float): Length of base edge (>0).\n        height (float): Vertical height (>0).\n\n    Returns:\n        float: Total surface area.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If base_edge <= 0 or height <= 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if base_edge <= 0 or height <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Both base_edge and height must be positive numbers.\")\n    base_area = base_edge * base_edge\n    lateral_area = 2 * base_edge * height\n    return base_area + lateral_area"}
