{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "import collections.abc\nfrom typing import Any, List, Sequence\ndef split_Arr(sequence: Sequence[Any], n: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Split the input sequence at index ``n`` and append the first part to the end.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    sequence : Sequence[Any]\n        The sequence to be split. Must support indexing and slicing.\n    n : int\n        The index at which to split. Must satisfy 0 <= n <= len(sequence).\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    List[Any]\n        A new list with elements reordered as described.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If ``sequence`` is not a Sequence or ``n`` is not an int.\n    ValueError\n        If ``n`` is outside the valid range [0, len(sequence)].\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(sequence, collections.abc.Sequence):\n        raise TypeError(\"sequence must be a Sequence type\")\n\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n\n    seq_len = len(sequence)\n    if n < 0 or n > seq_len:\n        raise ValueError(f\"n must be in the range [0, {seq_len}]\")\n\n    first_part = sequence[:n]\n    second_part = sequence[n:]\n\n    return list(second_part) + list(first_part)"}
