{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\nfrom math import cos, sin\ndef polar_rect(r: float, theta: float) -> Tuple[Tuple[float, float], complex]:\n    \"\"\"Convert polar coordinates to rectangular coordinates and return the\n    complex representation.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    r : float\n        Radius (must be non\u2011negative).\n    theta : float\n        Angle in radians.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    Tuple[Tuple[float, float], complex]\n        First element is the original polar tuple (r, theta), second element is\n        the complex number x + yi.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If r or theta cannot be converted to float.\n    ValueError\n        If radius r is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        r_val = float(r)\n        theta_val = float(theta)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both r and theta must be float values.\")\n\n    if r_val < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius r must be non\u2011negative.\")\n\n    x = r_val * cos(theta_val)\n    y = r_val * sin(theta_val)\n    return ((r_val, theta_val), complex(x, y))"}
