{"task_id": "Mbpp/593", "solution": "def removezero_ip(ip: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Remove leading zeros from each octet of an IPv4 address.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    ip : str\n        The IPv4 address string to normalize. Must contain exactly four octets\n        separated by dots.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    str\n        The canonical IPv4 address with no leading zeros in any octet.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If the input is not a valid IPv4 address: wrong number of octets,\n        non\u2011numeric characters, or octet values outside the 0\u2011255 range.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> removezero_ip('192.168.001.010')\n    '192.168.1.10'\n    >>> removezero_ip('0.0.0.0')\n    '0.0.0.0'\n    \"\"\"\n    parts = ip.split('.')\n    if len(parts) != 4:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Invalid IPv4 address: '{ip}'. Reason: Expected 4 octets, got {len(parts)}.\"\n        )\n    normalized_parts = []\n    for idx, part in enumerate(parts, start=1):\n        if not part.isdigit():\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Invalid IPv4 address: '{ip}'. Reason: Octet {idx} ('{part}') contains non\u2011digit characters.\"\n            )\n        num = int(part)\n        if not 0 <= num <= 255:\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Invalid IPv4 address: '{ip}'. Reason: Octet {idx} ('{part}') out of range (0-255).\"\n            )\n        normalized_parts.append(str(num))\n    return '.'.join(normalized_parts)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "def diff_even_odd(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the difference between the first even number and the first odd number in the list.\n    The difference is calculated as first_even - first_odd.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    numbers : list[int]\n        List of integers to search.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        The difference (first_even - first_odd).\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If the list contains no even number or no odd number.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for n in numbers:\n        if first_even is None and n % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = n\n        if first_odd is None and n % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = n\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n\n    if first_even is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No even number found in the list.\")\n    if first_odd is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No odd number found in the list.\")\n\n    return first_even - first_odd"}
