{"task_id": "Mbpp/723", "solution": "from collections.abc import Sequence\nfrom typing import Any\ndef count_same_pair(list_a: Sequence[Any], list_b: Sequence[Any]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count the number of indices where two sequences have equal elements.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    list_a : Sequence[Any]\n        First sequence to compare.\n    list_b : Sequence[Any]\n        Second sequence to compare.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Number of matching indices.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If either argument is not a sequence.\n    ValueError\n        If sequences are of unequal length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_a, Sequence) or not isinstance(list_b, Sequence):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a sequence (list, tuple, etc.)\")\n\n    if len(list_a) != len(list_b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Sequences must be of equal length\")\n\n    count = 0\n    for a, b in zip(list_a, list_b):\n        if a == b:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/724", "solution": "def power_base_sum(base: int, power: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the sum of decimal digits of base raised to the given power.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    base : int\n        Non\u2011negative integer base (>= 0).\n    power : int\n        Non\u2011negative integer exponent (>= 0).\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Sum of the decimal digits of base ** power.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If either argument is not an integer or is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(base, int) or not isinstance(power, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"base and power must be integers\")\n    if base < 0 or power < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"base and power must be non\u2011negative\")\n\n    result = pow(base, power)\n    return sum(int(ch) for ch in str(result))"}
