{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "import math\ndef is_perfect_square(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if n is a perfect square, False otherwise.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n is negative or exceeds the 32\u2011bit signed integer maximum.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> is_perfect_square(16)\n        True\n        >>> is_perfect_square(20)\n        False\n        >>> is_perfect_square(-1)\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n            ...\n        ValueError: Input must be non-negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be non-negative.\")\n    if n > 2_147_483_647:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input exceeds 32-bit signed integer maximum.\")\n    root = math.isqrt(n)\n    return root * root == n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/804", "solution": "def _has_even_element(nums):\n    \"\"\"Return True if any element in `nums` is even.\"\"\"\n    for val in nums:\n        if val % 2 == 0:\n            return True\n    return False\ndef is_product_even(nums: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determine if the product of all integers in the list is even.\n\n    Parameters:\n        nums (List[int]): List of integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if product is even, False otherwise.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any element in nums is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(nums)\n    if not nums:\n        # By design, empty list yields True\n        return True\n    return _has_even_element(nums)"}
